Fontconfig and Windows fonts

Install:
  Install missing Fontconfig tools and copy Windows fonts that are absent from the destination; refresh the font cache after copying.

Upgrade:
  Update installed Fontconfig tools and refresh changed copies of previously installed Windows fonts; refresh the font cache after copying.

Status:
  Report the Fontconfig package version, copied font count and source availability.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Source: /mnt/c/Windows/Fonts
  Destination: ~/.local/share/fonts/windows
  Copy TTF, TTC and OTF files directly from the source directory; skip copying when the source is unavailable.
  Install preserves existing copies; upgrade updates existing copies without adding or removing fonts.
